l":"Cash conversion","value":null,"unit":"\u00d7","status":"na","read":null,"meaning":"Operating cash flow is not a meaningful concept for a lender (deposits & loans dominate the cash statement).","why_useful":"For banks, earnings quality is read from asset quality / provisioning instead (not in MVP-1).","why_it_can_fail":null},{"label":"Balance-sheet safety","value":null,"unit":"","status":"na","read":null,"meaning":"A bank is structurally levered (deposits are its raw material); D/E & interest-cover don't apply.","why_useful":"Read bank safety from capital adequacy (CAR) and NPAs instead (not in MVP-1).","why_it_can_fail":null},{"label":"Earnings momentum","value":25.71,"unit":"% YoY","status":"ok","read":"Profit up 26% YoY \u2014 modest.","meaning":"Trailing-twelve-month net profit vs the year-ago TTM (and whether the YoY rate is rising = 'accelerating').","why_useful":"Improving, accelerating earnings tend to drive re-rating; falling profit warns of a deteriorating business.","why_it_can_fail":"TTM can be lumpy for cyclicals/one-offs; cross-check the multi-year trend on the Fundamentals tab."}]},"valuation":{"ok":true,"is_bank":true,"pe_now":null,"pe_percentile":null,"median_pe":null,"earnings_yield_pct":null,"pb":0.92,"ev_ebitda":null,"quality_score":36.0,"pat_cagr_5y_pct":21.3,"peg":null,"cheapness":{"status":"na","read":null},"expectations":null,"cyclical_caveat":null,"meaning":"P/E percentile = where today's price-to-earnings sits within the stock's own last-10-yr range (low = cheap vs its past). Paired with the Quality score and 5-yr profit growth so a cheap multiple is judged against business strength, not in isolation.","why_useful":"Cheapness only matters relative to quality and growth \u2014 a low P/E on a declining or peak-cyclical business is a trap, not a bargain.","why_it_can_fail":"P/E breaks for loss-makers / one-offs; for banks use P/B not EV/EBITDA; a multiple cheap vs history can stay cheap if the business has structurally de-rated."},"ownershi